Task: Configuring Secure SSH Access to an EC2 Instance
Solution: 1) Create an EC2 instance (with no keypair)
          2) Generate a key pair form the host (aws-client):
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 2048 -f /root/.ssh/id_rsa -N ""
cat /root/.ssh/id_rsa.pub
          3) Add the public key to EC2 ssh key directory:
sudo mkdir -p /root/.ssh
sudo vi /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
sudo chmod 700 /root/.ssh
sudo chmod 600 /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
sudo chown -R root:root /root/.ssh
          4) test by ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_rsa root@publicIP
